{"name":"Cheviot","hex":"#f6f2e8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Cheviot","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sheep of a hardy short-wool breed reared on the Cheviot Hills."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The Cheviot, a hill, the highest point in the Cheviot Hills in Kirknewton parish and Earle parish, Northumberland, England .","A locality in the Shire of Murrindindi, Victoria, Australia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Cheviot"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Cheviot","blocks":[{"text":"The Cheviot is an extinct volcano and the highest summit in the Cheviot Hills and in the county of Northumberland. Located in the extreme north of England, it is a 1+1⁄4-mile (2-kilometre) walk from the Scottish border and, with a height of 2,674 feet above sea-level, is located on the northernmost few miles of the Pennine Way, before the descent into Kirk Yetholm."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Cheviot0410a.jpg/330px-Cheviot0410a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Cheviot"},{"title":"Cheviot, Victoria","blocks":[{"text":"Cheviot is a locality in Victoria, Australia in the Shire of Murrindindi local government area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/CheviotRailwayTunnel.JPG/330px-CheviotRailwayTunnel.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheviot%2C_Victoria"},{"title":"Cheviot (New Zealand electorate)","blocks":[{"text":"Cheviot was a parliamentary electorate in the Canterbury region of New Zealand, from 1858 to 1890. It was named after what was then one of the country's largest sheep stations, Cheviot Hills."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheviot_(New_Zealand_electorate)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Hen_Hole_-_geograph.org.uk_-_48620.jpg/500px-Hen_Hole_-_geograph.org.uk_-_48620.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Hen_Hole_-_geograph.org.uk_-_48620.jpg/500px-Hen_Hole_-_geograph.org.uk_-_48620.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hen Hole, a gorge that marks the start of the College valley on the Cheviot.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHen_Hole_-_geograph.org.uk_-_48620.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Mt_Etna_and_Catania1.jpg/500px-Mt_Etna_and_Catania1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Mt_Etna_and_Catania1.jpg/1280px-Mt_Etna_and_Catania1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Mt_Etna_and_Catania1.jpg/500px-Mt_Etna_and_Catania1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"During the geological era in which it was active, The Cheviot volcano may have been similar in size to Mount Etna on Sicily (pictured).[20]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMt_Etna_and_Catania1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/B17_Undercarriage_The_Cheviot.jpg/500px-B17_Undercarriage_The_Cheviot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/B17_Undercarriage_The_Cheviot.jpg/1280px-B17_Undercarriage_The_Cheviot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/B17_Undercarriage_The_Cheviot.jpg/500px-B17_Undercarriage_The_Cheviot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The landing gear of a B-17 bomber that crashed in World War